<title>ARGENTINA: Steamy weather in Argentine crop zones after storm.</title>
<headline>Steamy weather in Argentine crop zones after storm.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine farmers were enjoying steamy weather Monday after a stormy weekend in which damage to crops was largely avoided, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;The only problem was that there was a bit of wind near Mar del Plata which might have flattened some maize, but not a significant quantity,&quot; a trader told Reuters.</p>
<p>He said it had rained throughout crop areas Sunday night and Monday morning, with particularly heavy falls in Cordoba province. In general the rains were good for developing maize, soybeans and sunflowers, but will cause some further delays in what little remains of the wheat harvest.</p>
<p>The Argentine government's Meteorological Service and Weather Services Corp forecast hot, unstable weather throughout crop areas Monday, with highs ranging from 84-94 F (29-34 C).</p>
<p>((--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
